This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Two of the rule's three shapes apply, either alone being sufficient.

Its SUBJECT is scripts/backlog-rotate.sh, which is not installed: install.sh's copy loop
derives from core/scripts/ and never touches the repo-root scripts/. It also reads the
repository's own docs/backlog.md as a false-positive corpus, and a consumer tree gets no
docs/backlog.md. On a consumer this fixture would resolve no tool and no corpus, and could
only pass.

It is also a MUTATION BATTERY: it builds sandbox roots under mktemp holding sed-mutated
copies of scripts/backlog-rotate.sh and a copy of
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/lib.sh, and asserts each mutant kills the arm it
targets.

The consumer's equivalent ledger is the push-candidate ledger under
_bmad-output/ai-dlc-update/, whose own fixtures (ledger-reverify, ledger-rotate,
ledger-status-vocabulary, ledger-reverify-unfalsifiable) ship and cover it. This one must
not be confused for those, and its sibling core/fixtures/backlog-ledger/ carries the same
declaration for the same reason.
